                <pb facs="0329" n="236" sameAs="frus:frus1935v04/pg236"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">714.18/35: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Guatemala</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Hanna</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Guatemala</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-02-28T17:00:00-06:00">February 28, 1935—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 8:17 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>8. My telegram February 28, 4 p.m. I fear President Ubico will be most reluctant
                    to adopt the procedure outlined in Minister Sack’s telegram of February 28, 10
                    a.m., but he may accept it if I am authorized to propose it as the suggestion of
                    the Secretary of State. I hope the Department can send me a telegram in that
                    sense which I can show to President Ubico.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hanna</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
